### Rewards Must Be Economically Sustainable

Every tangible reward creates a cost for Essentials Mart.

Reward Intelligence must therefore evaluate the expected business cost before authorising a reward.

The objective is not to maximise the value distributed to customers.

The objective is to maximise meaningful customer appreciation while maintaining sustainable economics.

---

### Rewards Must Be Valuable to the Recipient

The most appropriate reward is not necessarily the most expensive reward.

A low-cost benefit that is highly relevant to a customer may create greater appreciation than a more expensive generic benefit.

Examples include:

