```

The system does not automatically message the customer simply because another agent has detected an opportunity.

The opportunity must pass through contextual and trust evaluation.

---

# Enterprise Learning Memory

The Learning Engine should maintain structured learning memory across:

* customer;
* household;
* product;
* store;
* service;
* region;
* country;
* enterprise.

Learning memory must preserve provenance.

The system should know:

* where a learning signal originated;
* when it occurred;
* how reliable it is;
* whether it has been corroborated;
* what decision it influenced;
* and whether the resulting decision succeeded.

---

# Learning Governance

Learned information must not silently become permanent truth.

Important learned patterns should have:

* provenance;
* confidence;
* recency;
* evidence count;
* expiry or review conditions;
* responsible domain;
* model/rule version.

This prevents outdated assumptions from becoming permanent customer profiles.

---

