# 24. Anti-Corruption Principle

When two domains use different internal models for the same real-world concept, an explicit translation boundary should exist.

Example:

```text
Commerce Order Model
        ↓
Integration Contract
        ↓
Finance Transaction Model
```

Neither domain should be forced to adopt the other's internal representation.

This protects domain autonomy and prevents one domain's internal model from contaminating another domain.

---

# 25. Failure Isolation

Failure in one domain should not unnecessarily disable unrelated capabilities.

For example:

```text
Learning Engine unavailable
        ↓
Shopping continues
```

and:

```text
Recognition unavailable
        ↓
Checkout continues
```

Non-critical intelligence must degrade gracefully.

Critical transactional capabilities should remain operational according to their own availability requirements.

---

# 26. AI Failure Isolation

AI must not become a single point of failure for core commerce.

If AI services become unavailable, customers should still be able to:

* browse;
* shop;
* checkout;
* pay;
