# 44. Intelligence Does Not Become Autonomous Authority

The following architectural prohibition is established:

> **No Intelligence Engine may independently grant itself authority that has not been explicitly assigned to it by the enterprise architecture.**

An engine cannot decide:

> "Because I can predict this, I may now control this."

Capability does not imply authority.

